=1150 height=364 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >At least I\u2019m not completely alone. <strong>H.A.P.P.Y.</strong>, the ship\u2019s over-eager AI, insists on tagging along. With its \u201chelp,\u201d I shift tetrominos to reshape the terrain, blast enemies when things get hairy, and puzzle my way through whatever obstacles this planet throws at me.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Along the way, I stumble across eccentric crewmates and passengers, uncover secrets best left buried, and try to keep what\u2019s left of my sanity. The game is turn-based, which gives me time to plan every move\u2026 though if I overthink it, I\u2019ll probably just dig myself into a hole.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1349680/extras/7caf910cd651e4b21270341e5422649f.avif?t=1759849293\" width=1176 height=585 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The adventure unfolds chapter by chapter, each one packed with new puzzles, hazards, and plenty of questionable life choices. <strong>Chapter 1</strong> is just the beginning \u2014 and trust me, the crew has more ways to ruin my day than this planet ever could.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1349680/extras/storepage_footer?t=1759849293\" /></span></p>","developers":["Steve Welz"],"genres":[{"description":"Action","id":"1"},{"description":"Adventure","id":"25"},{"description":"Casual","id":"4"},{"description":"Indie","id":"23"},{"description":"Early Access","id":"70"}],"header_image":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1349680/127d37e0ca89fbf54cce32294170cb5ec0e0a77f/header.jpg?t=1759849293","is_free":false,"linux_requirements":[],"mac_requirements":{"minimum":"<strong>Minimum:<